      "summary": {
        "headline": "First-Class Mail categories received by all households showed long-term declines across the FY2010 methodology break, with various projected trajectories through FY2028.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class advertising received (ads only) fell across the FY2010 methodology break by 6,235.0 millions of pieces or 65.8 percent from 2000 to 2023.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-advertising",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2010,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class advertising received (ads only) decreased since the latest break by 2,879.0 millions of pieces or 47.1 percent from 2010 to 2023, and fell by 268.0 millions of pieces or 7.6 percent from 2018 to 2023.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-advertising",
            "years": [
              2010,
              2018,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class advertising received (ads only) is projected at 3,236.0 millions of pieces in 2024 with an 80% prediction interval 2,737.0 to 3,735.0.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-advertising",
            "years": [
              2024
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class correspondence received fell across the FY2010 methodology break by 6,606.0 millions of pieces or 33.9 percent from 2000 to 2023.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-correspondence",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2010,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class correspondence received decreased since the latest break by 3,131.0 millions of pieces or 19.6 percent from 2010 to 2023, and fell by 1,911.0 millions of pieces or 12.9 percent from 2018 to 2023.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-correspondence",
            "years": [
              2010,
              2018,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class correspondence received is projected at 13,068.0 millions of pieces in 2024 with an 80% prediction interval 12,694.0 to 13,442.0.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-correspondence",
            "years": [
              2024
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class transaction mail received fell across the FY2010 methodology break by 9,635.0 millions of pieces or 39.3 percent from 2000 to 2023.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-transactions",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2010,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class transaction mail received decreased since the latest break by 8,384.0 millions of pieces or 36.0 percent from 2010 to 2023, and fell by 4,017.0 millions of pieces or 21.3 percent from 2018 to 2023.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-transactions",
            "years": [
              2010,
              2018,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "For All households, First-Class transaction mail received is projected at 13,927.0 millions of pieces in 2024 with an 80% prediction interval 13,204.0 to 14,650.0.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-transactions",
            "years": [
              2024
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "Beginning in 2010, diary data were restated because of changes in weighting methodology (Appendix A8 table notes). Values before 2010 use the earlier weighting.",
          "From the FY2024 report, results are published as pieces per household per year, and the survey contractor changed (NuStats to RCF). The FY2024 report restated 2014-2023 on its own basis, so its values for those years can differ slightly from earlier reports (e.g. bills paid by mail in 2014: 34% in FY2023, 33% in FY2024).",
          "FY2025 used a new survey design (renamed the Household Mail Survey); Q1 was still covered by the old survey. Age bands changed to Under 45 / 45-64 / 65+ (previously 18-34 / 35-54 / 55+), and 'Large MSA' was redefined in January 2025 from the top 30 metros to metros of 1 million or more."
        ]
